  "body": "## What changed\n`crates/app/tests/sinker_undersize.rs` wrote the rough and finish CL texts of #1136's pair concatenated into one golden, `sinker_rough_finish_pair.cl`, with two `; HSMW-CL` headers. The CL text reader merges them into one path, so `camcraft-cl`'s `headless_bin::cl_text_round_trips_every_golden` failed on main (batch gate on a5d1a763).\n\nEach pass is now its own golden: `sinker_rough_finish_pair_rough.cl` and `sinker_rough_finish_pair_finish.cl`. The bytes are the same two streams split at the second header, and the old file is removed. Test-only; no product code changes.\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test sinker_undersize`: 7 passed (the pair test writes or compares both goldens).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-cl --test headless_bin`: 3 passed, including `cl_text_round_trips_every_golden`.\n\n## Not exercised\nNothing else touches these files.\n\nChangelog: none (test-only)\n\nFixes #1374\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
